    "created_at": "2022-07-14T08:13:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-14T08:13:48Z",
    "body": "As a web-dev I think I'd kind of prefer that the behavior of the 2D context matches the CSS one as much as possible.  \r\n\r\nWould it be an option to add the missing longhands (`ctx.fontFamily`, `ctx.fontSize`, `ctx.fontStyle`, and `ctx.fontWeight`) and let `ctx.font` act the same as the CSS shorthand?\r\nSo when we update `ctx.font` all the affected longhands get updated, and when the longhands are updated, `ctx.font` getter tries to render it or returns `\"\"` when it can't, like I believe `getComputedStyle(elem).font` is supposed to do (though [the lack of interop' here](https://jsfiddle.net/vyw9po7L/) is quite problematic, I admit).   \r\nIf all the longhands are available, I believe `ctx.font`'s getter is less critical and it's ok for it to fail.\r\n\r\n___\r\nPs: cc @whatwg/canvas and particularly @yiyix ",
